(menhir
 (modules Trees_Parse Annotations_Parse Mpileup_Parse)
 (flags --dump --explain --automaton-graph --cmly))
(ocamllex Trees_Lex Annotations_Lex Mpileup_Lex)

; Everything below the thirteen toplevel modules is private: the two [_Base]
; modules, the [Annotations] scaffolding, the five per-format modules, and the
; lexers and parsers.  Sealing a module that something re-exports takes one
; precaution, because an unconstrained [include M] -- or a [module X = M.Y]
; alias -- re-exports M's contents as aliases INTO M, and an alias into a
; private module does not resolve; the compiler then says that some module "is
; an alias for BiOCamLib__M.X, which is missing".  Constraining the include
; copies the signature instead of aliasing it, which closes the door behind the
; module.  Where the signature is worth writing down -- the five format modules,
; whose surface is four lines and is checked against what they declare -- it is
; written down; where it is only scaffolding, [include (M: module type of M)]
; says "copy, do not alias" without repeating anything.
;
; Annotations.ml is itself sealed, in the house [include (struct ... end: sig
; ... end)] form, and the rule its signature obeys is that a public signature
; may not name a private module at all -- not as an alias, not through a [module
; type of], not as a module-type equation, because each of those leaves the
; consumer with something it must expand and cannot.  What lives only inside a
; sealed module is therefore written out; what has a public interface elsewhere
; is named ([AttrMap] is [Better.IntMap]).  Writing it out is the standing cost
; of sealing a module whose types are part of the API, and the reason to accept
; it is that the result is an interface rather than a re-export.

(library
 (libraries zarith)
 (public_name BiOCamLib)
 (name BiOCamLib)
 (private_modules
   Annotations_Base
   Annotations_Common
   Annotations_GFF3
   Annotations_GTF
   Annotations_GenBank
   Annotations_Tabular
   Annotations_Tbl
   Annotations_Lex
   Annotations_Parse
   Mpileup_Base
   Mpileup_Lex
   Mpileup_Parse
   Trees_Base
   Trees_Lex
   Trees_Parse))
